h(2, id: "examples") { 17. Examples }

h(3, id: "minimal-example") { 17.1 Minimal document }

codeblock(lang: "text", file: "hello.du", line_numbers: true, highlight: "1-3") {!
meta {
  title: "Hello"
}

h(1) { Hello }

p { First paragraph. b{Bold}, i{italic}, code{code}. }

list {
  item { An item }
}

hr {}
!}

h(3, id: "full-example") { 17.2 Features in this document }

list {
    item { meta, including title and the optional fields the generator reads }
    item { headings with explicit ids and one class }
    item { paragraphs }
    item { toc }
    item { lists, ordered lists, tasks, nested lists }
    item { quotes and a nested quote }
    item { tables, including a header row and an included fragment }
    item { the banner image }
    item { callouts of all four kinds }
    item { codeblock with lang, file, line numbers, and highlight ranges }
    item { raw HTML }
    item { display math and inline math }
    item { footnote references and definitions }
    item { include, both from the root file and from a child file }
    item { line comments }
}

raw {!
<aside class="callout callout-note">
  <div class="callout-title">Raw</div>
  <div class="callout-body">This aside was emitted by a raw block. It is not parsed as DocUP.</div>
</aside>
!}

h(3, id: "limits") { 17.3 Limits }

list {
    item { One meta block. }
    item { Include cycles are rejected. }
    item { Inline, list, and quote nesting share a cap of 64. }
    item { Nested list or quote must be the last child of its parent body. }
    item { No block inside a paragraph. A list inside a p body is plain text. }
    item { Child-file meta is not merged. }
    item { A raw scope ends at the first bang-brace. }
}

h(3, id: "build-these-pages") { 17.4 Building these pages }

p {
    The root file is code{index.du}. From the docs directory:
}

codeblock(lang: "text") {!
docup build index.du
docup build index.du -o index.html
docup watch index.du --port 8080
!}

p {
    Output defaults to code{index.html} next to the input.
}

h(4, id: "heading-levels") { Heading levels }

p {
    Levels 1 through 6 are valid. This section is level 4.
}

h(5, id: "heading-level-5") { Level 5 }

p {
    Level 5.
}

h(6, id: "heading-level-6") { Level 6 }

p {
    Level 6. Compiler version code{0.2.0}.
}
